 repo's `project` key and `name`) plus `github.labels`. `config.Config.Tracker` selects the implementation; Jira settings are validated only when Jira is selected. The CLI grows a `Preflight`/`Setup` seam so `check`, `init` and `run` work for either tracker. The dispatcher is untouched.\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-phase-7-github-issues-tracker.md:9:**Tech Stack:** Go 1.27 stdlib; GitHub REST API 2022-11-28 (`/repos/{o}/{r}/issues`, `/issues/{n}`, `/issues/{n}/comments`, `/issues/{n}/labels`, `/labels`).\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-phase-7-github-issues-tracker.md:26:internal/config/config.go                 + Tracker (\"jira\"|\"github\"), RepoConfig.Project (jira_project alias), GitHubConfig.Labels\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-phase-7-github-issues-tracker.md:30:internal/tracker/ghissues/admin.go        Check (token, repos, labels), EnsureLabels\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-phase-7-github-issues-tracker.md:51:GitHubConfig.Labels GitHubLabels `yaml:\"labels\"`\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-phase-7-github-issues-tracker.md:52:type GitHubLabels struct { Ready, InProgress, NeedsInfo, InReview, NeedsHuman string } // defaults hive:ready …\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-phase-7-github-issues-tracker.md:57:- [ ] **Step 1: Tests** — `TestTrackerGithubSkipsJiraValidation` (config with `tracker: github`, no `jira:` block, `HIVE_GITHUB_TOKEN=gh` → valid; defaults labels), `TestJiraProjectAliasPopulatesProject`, `TestTrackerUnknownRejected`.\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-phase-7-github-issues-tracker.md:59:- [ ] **Step 3: Starter** — add a `tracker: jira` line at the top with a comment: \"or github: state is carried by labels, the claim by a hidden marker in the issue body; jira.* is then ignored and HIVE_GITHUB_TOKEN must have issues: write\". Rename the comment on `jira_project` → `project`.\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-phase-7-github-issues-tracker.md:60:- [ ] **Step 4:** `go vet ./... && go test -race ./... && golangci-lint run` → commit `feat(config): tracker selection; repos[].project (jira_project alias); github labels`.\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-phase-7-github-issues-tracker.md:76:func (c *Client) Poll(ctx) ([]tracker.Ticket, error)    // per repo: GET /repos/{r}/issues?state=open&labels=<ready>&per_page=100 (paginate via Link header, max 5 pages), skipping pull requests (issues with \"pull_request\" key)\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-phase-7-github-issues-tracker.md:79:func (c *Client) Transition(ctx, key, to tracker.State) error  // DELETE other hive labels, POST target label\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-phase-7-github-issues-tracker.md:80:// Ticket mapping: Key \"<P>-<n>\", Summary title, Description body without marker, Status = the hive:* label present or \"open\", URL html_url, Labels all names, Comments (author login), Claim from marker, Updated updated_at\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-phase-7-github-issues-tracker.md:107:- [ ] **Step 2: Implement** with a `beforeReadBack` hook like the Jira client. Body PATCH is `{\"body\": ...}` only — never touch title or labels here.\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-phase-7-github-issues-tracker.md:112:### Task 4: Check, EnsureLabels, CLI wiring, docs\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-phase-7-github-issues-tracker.md:122:type CheckReport struct { User string; Repos []string; MissingLabels map[string][]string; SampleTickets int }\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-phase-7-github-issues-tracker.md:124:func (c *Client) Check(ctx) (CheckReport, error)     // GET /user; per repo GET /repos/{r} (must exist, permissions.push or has_issues); GET /repos/{r}/labels (paginated) vs the five configured; Poll count\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-phase-7-github-issues-tracker.md:125:func (c *Client) EnsureLabels(ctx) (created int, err error)   // POST /repos/{r}/labels for each missing, with colours and descriptions\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-phase-7-github-issues-tracker.md:130:- `check`: `-jira` becomes `-live` (keep `-jira` as a hidden alias) and runs whichever tracker's preflight; `init -github` calls `EnsureLabels`.\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-phase-7-github-issues-tracker.md:131:- `githubPreflight` prints: user, repos ok, missing labels (with \"run `hivedispatch init -github`\"), matched tickets.\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-phase-7-github-issues-tracker.md:133:Docs: `docs/setup.md` gets a \"GitHub Issues instead of Jira\" section (token permissions: Issues read/write, Pull requests read/write, Contents read; labels; how to trigger from the phone: add `hive:ready`); `docs/config.md` rows for `tracker`, `repos[].project`, `github.labels.*`; README states both trackers; decisions entry.\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-phase-7-github-issues-tracker.md:135:- [ ] **Step 1: Tests** for Check (missing labels reported per repo; PR-typed issues not counted) and EnsureLabels (creates only missing; `httptest`), plus a `cmd` test that `check` with `tracker: github` and no token fails with a hint mentioning `gh auth login` and `HIVE_GITHUB_TOKEN`.\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-20-phase-7-github-issues-tracker.md:144:**Spec coverage:** second `Tracker` implementation ✔; claim protocol identical in shape (write, read-back, heartbeat, stale reclaim) ✔; phone-driven steering (labels) ✔; setup automation (`init -github`) ✔; preflight parity with Jira ✔.\ninternal/tracker/tracker.go:68:\tLabels      []string\ninternal/tracker/ghissues/issues_test.go:19:  \"labels\": [{\"name\": \"hive:ready\"}, {\"name\": \"bug\"}],\ninternal/tracker/ghissues/issues_test.go:37:\tif tk.Status != \"hive:ready\" || len(tk.Labels) != 2 {\ninternal/tracker/ghissues/issues_test.go:38:\t\tt.Errorf(\"status/labels = %q %v\", tk.Status, tk.Labels)\ninternal/tracker/ghissues/issues_test.go:51:\t\tif r.URL.Query().Get(\"labels\") != \"hive:ready\" || r.URL.Query().Get(\"state\") != \"open\" {\ninternal/tracker/ghissues/issues_test.go:55:\t\t\t_, _ = w.Write([]byte(`[{\"number\": 2, \"title\": \"two\