{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfEBk6PypYWhgiLRpNJpF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Two commits on `hive/SCRUM-5`, working tree clean, nothing pushed. `go vet ./...`, `go test -race ./...` (0 failures), and `golangci-lint run ./...` (0 issues) all pass module-wide.\n\n## Summary\n\n**What changed**\n\n- **`internal/config`** — new optional `github.project` block: `owner`, `number` (from the board URL), `field` (default `Status`), and `columns` (one option name per state, defaulting to `Ready` / `In Progress` / `Needs Info` / `In Review` / `Needs Human`). `Enabled()` is false when the block is absent; when present, owner and number are validated with hints pointing at the URL.\n- **`internal/tracker/ghissues/project.go`** (new) — GraphQL client for Projects v2, posted to `graphql` resolved against `api_url` (so GHES lands on `/api/graphql`). Resolves the board once via `repositoryOwner(login:) { ... on ProjectV2Owner { projectV2 } }` (works for users and orgs without an owner-type setting), caches it, and re-reads once if a column is missing so a column added while the worker runs is picked up. `INSUFFICIENT_SCOPES` errors tell the user `gh auth refresh -s project`.\n- **`Transition`** — after the label swap, when a board is configured: finds the issue's existing item on that board (via the REST `node_id`), adds it with `addProjectV2ItemById` if missing, then sets the option with `updateProjectV2ItemFieldValue`. A board failure returns an error naming the label that did land; the dispatcher already logs transition errors rather than failing the run, so labels stay authoritative and the board is a mirror.\n- **`Check` / `check -live`** — resolves the board and reports its title, missing columns, or why it was unreachable; any of those fails `OK()`.\n- **Docs** — starter config comment block, a \"A GitHub Projects board\" subsection in `docs/setup.md` (including the extra `project` token scope), and a `docs/decisions.md` entry recording the mirror-not-owner decision and the alternatives rejected (polling the board, rolling back labels, auto-creating options).\n\n**Tests** — config defaults/validation; tracker tests using a fake `/graphql` handler covering add-then-move, no second add on the next transition, no GraphQL calls at all without the block, missing-column refresh, scope-error hint, and `Check` reporting for found/missing-columns/unreachable boards.\n\n**Not done / to note** — columns are not created automatically (GitHub's `updateProjectV2Field` replaces the whole option list, so it's left to the user; `check -live` says exactly which are missing). For your board at `github.com/users/thomasmeadows/projects/2`, the config is `github.project.owner: thomasmeadows`, `number: 2`, plus column names matching your board — and the token needs the `project` scope, which the default `gh auth login` token does not include."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":413,"cache_read_input_tokens":106607,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":413},"output_tokens":732,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2daaed25-284e-4780-838f-5b169e1711d5","uuid":"867f0be9-ad36-49a5-891c-e6d2fd4ba368","timestamp":"2026-09-20T06:04:16.284Z","request_id":"req_011CfEBk5oWP97GKuHTpEGWE"}
